# Amahi-kai sudoers rules for the app user (amahi).
# Installed as /etc/sudoers.d/amahi-kai by bin/amahi-install and bin/amahi-update, only
# after `visudo -cf` accepts it. Design: docs/plans/privileged-helper.md
#
# Everything that needs root goes through the root helper, which checks each request and
# logs it to /var/log/amahi-kai/helper.log: user accounts, Samba, share folders, services,
# the hostname, dnsmasq, swap, reboot/power off, data drives, Greyhole, package installs,
# the Cloudflare Tunnel, Tailscale, the security audit's fixes, drive temperatures,
# ZFS pools, Docker apps, starting System Update and checking for updates. It is the only
# rule: anything else that needs root becomes a helper operation.

# Privileged helper (libexec/amahi-helper)
amahi ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/amahi-helper
